        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Severe aortic stenosis, TAVI or surgical valve replacement performed</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent admission of your 77-year-old male patient to our cardiology department. He presented with symptomatic severe aortic valve stenosis, confirmed by transthoracic echocardiography demonstrating a significantly reduced valve area with high transvalvular gradients. Pre-procedural workup included ECG, chest X-ray, blood tests, and CT imaging for procedural planning. Given his age and surgical risk profile, the heart team consensus favoured transcatheter aortic valve implantation (TAVI). The procedure was performed successfully without complications. Post-procedural echocardiography confirmed excellent prosthetic valve function. The patient recovered well, remained haemodynamically stable, and was mobilised with physiotherapy support. He is discharged in good condition on adjusted medication. Please arrange follow-up within four weeks, including echocardiographic assessment. Do not hesitate to contact us should any concerns arise.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
